From 18958c516702c2369e8cc471b0441b84d9b54dc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dfattal <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 19:17:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 62/71] inline-3d(Phase 1): give exclusion overlays an
 identity, merge per entry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An exclusion is a promise: this element's pixels stay 2D, out of the
weave. Two channels describe the page's exclusions and neither alone is
sufficient — the legacy CompositorFrameMetadata list is COMPLETE (Blink
walks the declaration list every frame) but its geometry trails the impl
scroll; a draw-time tracked-element rect is EXACT but only best-effort
present, because arbitrary overlay DOM has no guaranteed paint chunk.

The exclusion path had no way to combine them, only to choose, and the
choice was all-or-nothing per frame. Every exclusion whose element
happened to emit no chunk that frame was silently dropped — and a
dropped exclusion is not a no-op: its pixels stay in the tile's
side-by-side weave input and get woven, which is browser#22's blown-up
header. The drop stayed invisible because the diagnostics were throttled
by a single global counter, so the frames that dropped a row were
silenced by the frames that did not.

Identity is what lets the two be MERGED rather than chosen between. Each
exclusion now carries its element's TrackedElementId end to end, so the
aggregator can enumerate the complete channel and upgrade rows
individually from the exact one:

  - viz::TrackedElementFeature gains kInline3dOverlay, and
    XRDisplayLayer::excludeElement registers the excluded element on it.
    Deliberately WITHOUT carving a paint chunk out for the element:
    chunk presence stays best-effort, which is the whole point of a
    per-entry merge.
  - CompositorFrameMetadata::inline_3d_exclusion_rects becomes
    std::vector<viz::Inline3dExclusion> — {rect, id} — over mojom,
    traits, the cc commit/impl chain and the TreesInViz layer-context
    channel, with the round-trip unittest extended. The browser#28
    scrolling/fixed split keeps its exact shape (still cc-local); the
    browser#83 scroll patch now shifts e.rect and leaves the id alone.
  - The token comes from the same derivation 0060 introduced for weave
    targets (process salt + DOMNodeId), promoted to
    XRDisplayLayer::Inline3dTokenForElement. Same element, same token,
    always — which makes both the cross-layer de-dupe and registration
    idempotence structural rather than invariants to maintain.
  - XRSession de-dupes exclusions by id ACROSS layers. Page-global
    chrome excluded from every window on a page used to emit one
    identical entry per window and composite the same overlay resource
    that many times.
  - SurfaceAggregator enumerates the LEGACY list as the outer loop and
    upgrades a row's geometry only when a tracked entry with the same id
    exists. A tracked entry's presence can no longer suppress another
    row, and a row never mixes the two geometry bases.
  - The exclusion→quad join is now (namespace, sqs_layer_id) equality,
    last match winning; best-overlap survives as a logged fallback.
    Diagnostics are throttled PER ID — INLINE3D_ID_JOIN_MISS,
    INLINE3D_GEOM_FALLBACK, INLINE3D_UNCOMPOSITABLE (promoted but emits
    no resource quad: the backdrop-filter signature),
    INLINE3D_PROMOTION_LOST, INLINE3D_EXCL_ABSENT on a present→absent
    transition.
  - F-9: inline_3d_overlays is sorted back-to-front by the source quad's
    ordinal in the root pass, which is a real stacking order. The
    previous (y, x, w, h) geometric order was never one, so two
    overlapping overlays composited in whatever order their top edges
    happened to fall in.

kInline3dOverlay also gets kInline3dWeave's unclipped carve-out in
LayerTreeHostImpl::CollectTrackedElementRects: an exclusion's chunk
routinely lands on a layer that draws nothing, and intersecting against
that layer's empty visible_layer_rect zeroes the hole — the same bug
0026 fixed for canvases.

